    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the access drive so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with tall reflective posts on both sides to keep it visible at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Post a clearly visible property map or layout sign near the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence and detached structure.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the access drive so emergency vehicles can travel the full length without obstruction.\n• Keep the circular driveway clear of parked vehicles so arriving fire or medical units can pull forward and turn around without maneuvering around obstacles.\n• Designate and mark a specific staging area within the circular driveway where a second arriving unit can park without blocking the primary access route.\n• Keep the turnaround path of the circular driveway free of planters, decorative boulders, or landscaping features that reduce the usable turning radius for large vehicles.\n• Cut back vegetation growing against or directly adjacent to the detached structure to create clear space around all sides.\n• Thin dense vegetation along the access drive at intervals to reduce the risk of fire spreading along the route responders must use to reach the property.\n• Keep a gate or barrier at the single access point unlocked or equipped with a Knox Box so responders are not delayed gaining entry."
  },
