    "recommendations": "• Trim or remove shrubs that are growing directly against or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Thin the tree cluster near the structure to create open space between individual trees and between the trees and the house.\n• Remove low-hanging branches on trees close to the house so flames cannot climb from shrubs into the tree canopy.\n• Scatter or spread out the shrubs surrounding the structure so there is open ground between individual plants and the house.\n• Cut and remove dry or dead grass close to the house, especially where it connects ground cover to nearby shrubs or trees.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches so fire trucks and emergency vehicles can reach the house without obstruction.\n• Mow or cut grass along both sides of the driveway to reduce the chance of fire burning directly up to the road surface.\n• Move any wood piles, stored materials, or other burnable items away from the house and outbuildings.\n• Thin scattered trees across the property so open ground separates them rather than allowing branches to overlap and connect.\n• Clear shrubs and tall grass immediately around any detached structures or outbuildings on the property.\n• Maintain visible open ground between the green space areas and the house so there is a clear, unburned gap around the structure."
  },
